    "Sufmi Dasco Ahmad is increasingly cited as a primary candidate to replace Gibran Rakabuming Raka as vice president.",
    "Support for Dasco has emerged from various political factions and labor organizations, citing his compatibility with President Prabowo.",
    "The official timeline for the selection process requires President Prabowo to submit two candidate names by November 25."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political discourse in Indonesia is currently centered on the selection of a successor for the vice president, following the exit of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. While President Prabowo is tasked with finalizing the nomination, multiple political parties and organizations have expressed their perspectives on potential candidates. Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, a high-ranking official within the Gerindra Party, has gained significant attention as a viable choice, with backing from various entities including the PAN party and labor unions. Other figures such as Sugiono, Ahmad Muzani, and Yusril Ihza Mahendra are also mentioned as potential candidates within the ongoing evaluation process. With the inauguration of the new vice president delayed until December 9, legislative bodies have emphasized the need for a swift decision, requiring the president to present two nominees by late November for the transition to proceed.",
